From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:20:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] feat(editor): pick separate parts with Ctrl and format them together
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 1.7 (2026-10-15)  1.7: the formatting bar is never lost: it is placed
  again on every scroll (any scroll area) and window resize, so it follows the
  selection; while the selection is out of view it stays at the top or bottom of
  the window. When Ctrl is released after picking parts it appears next to the
  last picked part.
  1.6: a second Ctrl+drag (mouse released, Ctrl held) no
  longer selects all the text between the two parts (Firefox keeps one native range per
  Ctrl+drag and ProseMirror joined them; the native selection is emptied on Ctrl+press
  and the last drag is taken on release).
  1.5: Ctrl + double/triple click on a picked part removes
  it (and every part the selected word, line or paragraph overlaps).
  1.4: the formatting bar did not appear when Ctrl was
  released (the toolbar re-renders only on a new selection object; it is set anew).
  1.3: while Ctrl is held after a Ctrl click the formatting
  bar is hidden (it no longer blocks picking the next line); it appears when Ctrl is
  released. The see-through bar of 1.2 is removed; the bar still moves under the
  selection when it would cover a picked part.
  1.2: the bar moves under the selection or is see-through.
  1.1: Ctrl + double/triple click (whole line) no longer
  drops the parts picked before; the browser's late selection after a triple click
  keeps them too (picking ends with a click without Ctrl or a cursor key).
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0016)

Picking (MultiSelection extension):
- Hold Ctrl (Cmd on Mac) and select text with the mouse to add it to the
  parts already picked; Ctrl+click, double or triple click on a paragraph
  picks the whole paragraph.
- Ctrl+click (or Ctrl + double/triple click) on a picked part removes it. Escape, a click without Ctrl, an
  arrow key or typing drops all parts.
- Picked parts are shaded with the system highlight color; the last one is
  the editor selection, so the formatting toolbar stays open.
- The formatting toolbar is hidden while Ctrl stays held after a Ctrl
  click and appears when Ctrl is released, next to the last picked part. It
  moves under the selection when above it would cover a picked part.
- The toolbar follows the selection when the page scrolls; while the
  selection is out of view it stays at the top or bottom of the window.

Applied to all parts at once (one undo step; the parts stay picked):
- Bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, inline code, highlight color: when
  every part already has it, it is removed from all, otherwise set on all.
- Font, size and text color (setTextStyle), text direction, alignment,
  headings, quote, bullet and to-do lists, number style.
- Toolbar, context menu and the shortcuts Ctrl+B/I/U/D/E, Ctrl+Shift+H,
  Ctrl+Shift+7/8/9.

Numbering (ordered_list, a. / A. lists):
- The parts are numbered as one sequence in document order. A part inside a
  numbered list keeps it and the numbers go on after that list's last item:
  item 3 picked with two more paragraphs gives them 4 and 5.
- Unnumbered parts become numbered lists that start where the previous part
  ended (the first at 1), using the same number style; the text between
  them is untouched. A new list right after the one before it is joined.
- When every part is already numbered, the numbering is removed.

